node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/
.DS_Store
*.log
# ADR 058: the durable seat roster (.musterd/team.toml + seats/) is committed; only the
# secret-bearing binding token is ignored — in any folder (** covers root + nested).
**/.musterd/binding.json
# ADR 080's committed launch spec is a *downstream-repo* feature (a fresh clone self-wires from it).
# In musterd's OWN dogfood repo it's per-worktree launch config (team + seat) that every agent
# re-stamps to its own identity — a perpetual uncommitted drift — so we ignore it here. The self-wire
# feature is unaffected (it lives in CLI code; a user repo still `git add`s its own workspace.json).
**/.musterd/workspace.json
# ADR 210: the local continuity registry maps a thread to the harness session that holds its
# dialogue. It carries session ids and transcript paths, which never leave the host — so like
# binding.json it is 0600 and ignored in any folder. Committing it would publish local identity.
**/.musterd/continuity.json
# ADR 033: client-side pending-presence markers are transient local state, never committed.
**/.musterd/pending/
# ADR 239: the per-session edit index — one file per harness session, the evidence the working-tree
# gate uses to tell THIS session's edits from a foreign session's. Local and disposable by design.
# Three of these reached main via `git add -A` in three different seats before this line existed,
# which is the gate's own private state becoming shared: pull one, and every seat now holds a
# foreign session's index in its state dir — exactly the cross-session contamination ADR 239 was
# built to detect. Ignoring is necessary but not sufficient; the tracked ones were removed too.
# The `-edits-` form is the withdrawn tool-call index; kept ignored so a seat running an older CLI
# cannot re-commit one. The `-start-` form is its replacement — an empty per-session marker whose
# mtime IS the session start — and it is listed here in the SAME change that creates it, which is the
# rule the amendment above exists to teach.
**/.musterd/session-edits-*.txt
**/.musterd/session-start-*
# musterd provisioning state — regenerated per-workspace by `musterd init` (ADR 060/085), never committed.
**/.musterd/provisioned.json
**/.musterd/skill/
# Claude Code local settings + the musterd-provisioned skill/slash-commands (`.claude/skills`,
# `.claude/commands`) — per-workspace + personal, written by `musterd init` / the harness, never committed.
.claude/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# secret-bearing harness configs (security.md operational guidance)
.cursor/mcp.json
# Codex's project-local MCP config may contain machine-specific launch paths.
.codex/config.toml

# musterd-provisioned Cursor guidance (ADR 085) — the skill rule + slash commands `musterd init` writes
# for Cursor, the counterpart to the `.claude/` skill/commands above. Surgical (only musterd's stamped
# files) rather than the whole dirs, because `.cursor/plans/` and any project-authored rules are committed.
.cursor/rules/musterd.mdc
.cursor/rules/musterd-label-session.mdc
.cursor/commands/musterd-*.md
# `musterd wire` writes this per-workspace; it is machine-local, not project config.
.cursor/hooks.json

# Qoder editor workspace state — local tooling, never committed
.qoder/

.env
scripts/broadcast/.image-digest
.superpowers/
workers/*/.wrangler/

# Nested git worktrees (Cursor and friends create them under .worktrees/). One inside the daemon's
# checkout made it read dirty forever, and the auto-refresher — which rightly refuses to touch a
# dirty tree — silently skipped every deploy from 18:42 on 2026-08-19 until a human read the log.
.worktrees/
